/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365866 #edb/ref 1080 "$Bx{e}^{x}$ and $C{e}^{-x/2}(x+4)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365866 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365866 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7a1b1386-fefe-522a-9724-c7282fdf6830" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365867 #edb/ref 1080 "$Bx{e}^{-x}$ and $C{e}^{x/2}(x+\\frac{3}{2})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365867 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365867 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e9883a8c-7a90-5bdd-a094-5cb18a2dfc22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365868 #edb/ref 1080 "$Bx{e}^{-2x}$ and $C{e}^{x}(x-4)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365868 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365868 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8e3aea8a-e9e7-5796-bf9a-ff68da034ea5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366132 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186366133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366132 #edb/ref 1069 "q-41624" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366132 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366132 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {v}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}\\,,\\begin{bmatrix}| \\\\ {v}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{bmatrix}\\,,\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}\\}\n$$\n\nSuppose that $V=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ Given that $B$ is an orthogonal basis for $V,$ and that $B$ is derived from $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, what is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186366132 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "140b78de-e11f-5db2-951c-82c8f5734177" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366132 #edb/ref 1074 "We find an orthogonal basis $B$ of $V$ using the Gram-Schmidt process, as follows:\n\n**Step 1.** We set ${v}_{1}={a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n**Step 2.** We find the vector ${v}_{2}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1}\\}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{2} & ={a}_{2}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={a}_{2}-\\frac{{a}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{8}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3.** We find the vector ${v}_{3}$ orthogonal to $\\text{Span}\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2}\\}$ using the usual formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{3} & ={a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{1}}\\,{a}_{3}-{\\text{proj}}_{{v}_{2}}\\,{a}_{3} \\\\  & ={a}_{3}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}}{v}_{1}-\\frac{{a}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{{v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}}{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{6}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{18}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(4\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-8\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 6 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-\\frac{3}{2},$ $c=\\frac{3}{2},$ and $\\frac{a}{c}=\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2})}{(\\frac{3}{2})}=-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186366138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186366133 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 175921